  "disposition_rationale": "The proposed flow design translates the batch protocol into a continuous process using the available 15 mL two-stage reactor. The design respects the hard constraint of segregating TBHP and morpholine until the interstage point. However, the reaction involves hazardous reagents (TBHP, H2SO4) and generates exothermic oxidation products. While the stoichiometry and residence times are calculated based on the batch data, the specific kinetics of the bromine-mediated oxidation in flow and the potential for gas evolution (O2 from TBHP decomposition) require experimental validation to ensure pressure stability and conversion efficiency. Therefore, this is a feasible first experiment (SCREEN) rather than a fully validated execution (EXECUTE).",
