is 0.5 mL/min. Stage 1 (5 mL) provides 10 min residence time for oxidation. Stage 2 (10 mL) provides 20 min residence time for amidation. Total residence time is 30 min, matching the batch protocol.\", \"stage_parameters\": [{\"stage\": 1, \"volume_mL\": 5, \"residence_time_min\": 10, \"temperature_C\": 80, \"description\": \"Oxidation of Benzyl alcohol to Benzoyl bromide intermediate using TBHP/NaBr/H2SO4\"}, {\"stage\": 2, \"volume_mL\": 10, \"residence_time_min\": 20, \"temperature_C\": 80, \"description\": \"Amidation with Morpholine added at interstage\"}], \"reasoning_per_field\": {\"residence_time_min\": \"Matched to batch total time of 30 min.\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": \"Calculated to achieve 30 min residence time in 15 mL reactor: 15 mL / 30 min = 0.5 mL/min.\", \"temperature_C\": \"Set to 80 C as per batch protocol.\", \"concentration_M\": \"Maintained at 0.667 M for Benzyl alcohol to match batch conditions.\", \"BPR_bar\": \"Set to 5 bar to ensure liquid phase and handle potential gas evolution from TBHP decomposition.\", \"streams\": \"Stream A carries the oxidation mixture. Stream B carries morpholine, added via interstage pump to maintain segregation.\"}, \"literature_analogies\": \"Similar to flow oxidation of alcohols using TBHP and subsequent trapping with nucleophiles.\", \"engine_validated\": true, \"safety_flags\": [\"TBHP is a strong oxidant and can be explosive under certain conditions. Ensure proper pressure relief.\", \"H2SO4 is corrosive. Use PFA tubing.\", \"Exothermic reaction. Monitor temperature closely.\"], \"confidence\": 0.8}"
